    "reasoning": {
        "HF": {
            "root.model.layers.{i}.mamba.act": "The SiLU activation function in HF is explicitly defined as a module (nn.SiLU) but is fused into the CUDA kernel operations in vLLM's MambaMixer2 implementation. In vLLM, the activation is specified by the 'activation' string parameter and applied within the causal_conv1d operations, not as a separate module. This is a deliberate optimization for performance.",
            "root.model.layers.{j}.mamba_decoder.mamba.act": "Same as above - the SiLU activation is fused into kernel operations in vLLM and not represented as a separate module.",
            "root.model.rotary_emb": "In HF, there is a single Zamba2RotaryEmbedding module at the model level. In vLLM, rotary embeddings are created per-attention-layer within each shared transformer block (root.model.layers.{j}.shared_transformer.self_attn.rotary_emb), not at the model root level. This is an architectural difference in how RoPE is managed - vLLM instantiates it per attention layer for better modularization and integration with its serving infrastructure."
        },
        "vLLM": {
            "root.model.layers.{j}.shared_transformer.self_attn.dpa_list": "The dpa_list (dot-product attention list) in vLLM is a ModuleList container that holds Attention modules for managing attention computation with KV caching. In HF, attention is computed inline within the Zamba2Attention.forward() method. This is a vLLM infrastructure component for better integration with its serving system. Each dpa_list contains 6 elements corresponding to the 6 hybrid layers that share this transformer block.",
            "root.model.layers.{j}.shared_transformer.self_attn.dpa_list.{k}": "Individual Attention backend modules within dpa_list. These are vLLM-specific infrastructure components for managing attention computation with KV caching and different attention backends (FlashAttention, xFormers, etc.). Not present in HF where attention is computed inline within the forward method.",
            "root.model.layers.{j}.shared_transformer.self_attn.rotary_emb": "vLLM creates per-layer RotaryEmbeddingWrapper modules while HF uses a single model-level Zamba2RotaryEmbedding module. The vLLM approach allows for better modularization and potential per-layer customization, fitting better with vLLM's architecture for distributed inference. These wrapper modules don't contain learnable parameters but manage the rotary embedding computation.",
            "root.logits_processor": "The LogitsProcessor is a vLLM-specific component for post-processing logits during inference serving (e.g., for temperature scaling, top-k/top-p sampling optimizations, logit bias). HF does not have an equivalent built into the model architecture - logit processing is handled externally in the generation pipeline. This is an infrastructure difference between a serving engine (vLLM) and a training/inference library (HF)."
        }
    }
